WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.202
-I want to ask about this.

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:05.038
Because, um,
do you have a scuba background?

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:07.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because you went to an opening
of an aquarium in Missouri?

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:13.113
-Yes. Yeah, Johnny Morris opened
this beautiful wildlife museum.

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:14.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
Johhny Morris is the founder
of Bass Pro Shop.

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:16.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-And all of a sudden,

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
George Bush was there,
Jimmy Carter.

00:00:18.318 --> 00:00:20.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
They´re like, "oh, you want to
get in the shark tank?"

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m like, "no, I don´t want to
get in the shark tank."

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:23.523
They´re like, "no, no, no,
it would be really cool.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.058
Get in the shark tank with the
stingrays and everything else."

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:27.027
Next thing you know, I´m diving
in this tank.

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:29.195
I mean, I literally just showed
up to say hello.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
-To show my support

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the opening of the museum.
-And there you are.

00:00:31.898 --> 00:00:33.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
That´s, I guess,
a little stingray, right?

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Although, I don´t mean

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
to say little. If I saw that,
I´d be terrified.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:40.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s how that guy
Steve Irwin died.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-He got stabbed by a stingray.

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:44.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don´t think in, like,
an aquarium, though.

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:46.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-You know what?

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.180
I don´t think they´re, like,

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
really trainable animals,
either.

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:50.750
You know, like, "hey, this one´s
not a stinger."

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
That´s a stinger right there,
that thing on the back.

00:00:52.786 --> 00:00:54.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, that´s the little thing
that --

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:56.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I think they have to go
through a really --

00:00:56.156 --> 00:00:58.558
a long training before they let
them in the aquarium.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.326 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, anyway, I went there.
We´re trying to persuade

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:02.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
these guys to do
this Wahlburger partnership,

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.264 align:start size:94% position:6%
open restaurants in
these Bass Pro Shops.

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:05.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
´cause people go there for,
like, six hours,

00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they´re like, "yeah, we´re
really into the idea."

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:09.269
But now we´re in a tank, and we
still don´t have a Wahlburgers

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:11.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a Bass Pro Shop.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:13.840
-Oh, so this was -- you saw this
as a business opportunity,

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.108
and it totally backfired.

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:17.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You see what I do
to support my brand? Uh, yeah.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:20.313
And didn´t work out quite
the way I had hoped, so...

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:22.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And was it -- did it increase
the pressure to have

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:26.252
two ex-presidents watch you get
into a scuba tank?

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, they´re all sitting there
just having

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
hors d´oeuvres and cocktails
and looking...

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
Basically paying no attention
to me whatsoever --

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:33.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I guess that´s
the thing is --

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:35.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you can´t really see out.
-Yeah.

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:36.763 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know? And I´m like, "I´ve
got to go somewhere else

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
the same day."
-Yeah.

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:39.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, like, people
just kind of left me.

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.534
There was one other diver.
And they were just, like,

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.136 align:start size:94% position:6%
doing these signals.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:46.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I´m like, "I don´t know
scuba signals."

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:47.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Also, you can barely
tell it´s you.

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:49.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it´s not that exciting to
watch if someone´s like,

00:01:49.876 --> 00:01:51.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
"ladies and gentlemen,
Mark Wahlberg."

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:52.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
You´d be like,
"that could be anybody."

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:55.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
-You do get a -- which is

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.683
very surprising to me, because
you´ve been doing this so long

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.952
and you´re so recognizable.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:01.488
But you do get mistaken for one
actor more than other actors.

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:02.689
-Yes.
-You want to tell us who it is?

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:05.325
-My fellow Bostonian Matt Damon.
-Yeah.

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:07.760
-And by the way, your clip about
all the Boston movies...

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.028
-Oh...
-Was one of the funniest things

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:10.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´ve ever seen.
-[ Laughs ] Thank you.

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.632
-Much better Boston accent than
most of the people in Boston,

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:13.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
by the way,
so thank you for that.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:15.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, I don´t think
I´m top tier, but I do think

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:17.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m better than bottom.
-No, it´s -- it´s pretty high.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-It´s pretty high.

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:20.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
So anyway, yeah, he gets
recognized, you know, for me

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:23.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I get recognized for him.
But I never tell people.

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:25.145
I never correct anybody.
Somebody comes up and says,

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:26.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
"hey, I loved you
in ´The Bourne.´"

00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:28.014
I´m like, "thank you. I got
another one coming out soon."

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:31.017 size:84% position:42%
And I just keep going.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:32.519
It´s like, I start explaining --
-Yeah.

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:33.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I didn´t want to apologize.
-Yeah.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:36.089
-They think I´m offended.
I´m not offended at all.

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:38.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not a problem,
thank you very much.

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:40.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-I´ll see you later.

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:42.462
-You shot some of this movie,
"Daddy´s Home 2," in Boston.

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:43.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Is it exciting for you

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
to shoot in Boston?
-No.

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:48.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-Well, like, random people

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:50.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
showing up unannounced
and uninvited. No.

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, right,
´cause you have such...

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But every -- yeah, I have
a long history there.

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:56.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it´s nice to be able
to see my mom and stuff.

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:59.879
But, you know, like, everybody´s
like, "oh, I love Boston!"

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:02.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everybody who, like, went to
school to Boston

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:04.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
or spent a little time,
spent the summer in Nantucket

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:07.387
or on the cape, they love it.
You know, if you´ve been there,

00:03:07.387 --> 00:03:09.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, there´s a reason why
you wanna -- I mean,

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:11.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love going back. And I
appreciate that I can go back.

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:16.329
But I have people from my past,
some of them kind of sketchy

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:18.998
that´ll show up unannounced.
Like, my friends were, like,

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
plotting to steal
camera equipment before

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:24.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
on "The Perfect Storm."
And they were like,

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:25.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
"wow,
that thing looks expensive."

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.240 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m like, "yeah, it´s like
$250,000."

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.409
They´re like, "oh, let´s put it
in the trunk."

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:31.878
[ Laughter ]
I´m like, "who are you going to

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:35.548
"sell a Panovision camera to?
You´re going to sell it to

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
"George at the store
for 500 bucks

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:41.120
"and a free -- free pizza? He´s
not gonna be able to use it.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
They´re gonna --
they´re gonna catch you."

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:45.225
-I didn´t think of it that way.
That makes a lot of sense.

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:47.227
Hey, it´s always great to see
you. Congrats on the film.

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:48.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s a pleasure.
-Thanks for having me.

